  designNotes: "2026-09-02, Meshy AI attack (Meshy_AI_Parkside_Portrait_biped.zip,
    take \"Scene\", 92 frames / 3.03s) imported as Wushi_CrossSlash. Measured offline
    via AnimationMode.SampleAnimationClip on the live 4x \u6B66\u58EB, tracking BladeHitbox
    world Y / forward-reach / speed every 0.01 nt across the two swing phases. A
    genuine IN-PLACE two-hit combo - hips localZ stays 0.4-0.7 the whole clip, no
    lunge (unlike the removed DoubleCombo). Hit 1 (nt 0.19-0.30): blade crashes Y
    3.6 -> 1.0 across nt 0.20-0.26, speed peak 50 u/s at nt 0.20, sweeping forward
    reach -1.3 -> +3.3 - overhead diagonal downcut. deflectReaction ContinueCombo
    (first of the pair). Hit 2 (nt 0.68-0.76): forward extending sweep, reach 2.4
    -> 4.1m across nt 0.68-0.71, speed peak 44 u/s at nt 0.69, blade at torso height
    1.9-2.7 - the longest forward reach in the whole clip, connects cleanly from
    the ~3.5m standoff. deflectReaction Recoil (committed 2nd hit). No attackMotion
    / useRootMotion - attacks from the standoff, never enters the too-close kick
    circle.\n\n2026-09-02 \u7E8C 42, Play report (\"\u653B\u64CA\u6BD4\u8F03\u504F\u53F3...\u7A0D\u5FAE\u5F80\u5DE6\u8F49\u4E00\u9EDE\"
    + \"\u5169\u6BB5\u5288\u780D\u90FD\u662F\u63EE\u5200\u5B8C\u624D\u4EAE\u7D05\u8272\"):
    windows moved EARLIER so the red telegraph shows during the wind-up, not after
    the swing lands - hit 1 0.20-0.29 -> 0.13-0.28 (red lights while the blade is
    still raised), hit 2 0.68-0.76 -> 0.58-0.77 (red lights as the forward sweep
    loads). faceTargetSnapOnStart + facingYawOffsetDegrees -15 (the clip's swing
    is baked to the character's right; turn \u6B66\u58EB 15 deg left so it lands
    on a player dead ahead)."
